--- DELIVERABLE SUMMARY ---
Native WinUI 3 parity port of the web BackendStatusSection accordion, following the established
Source / Model / ViewModel / View seam (sibling: RateLimitStatusPanel, FleetTelemetryHealth):
  * BackendStatusSection.Source.cs — IBackendStatusSource + repository-backed BackendStatusSource: three
    independent cache-then-network reads through the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine, one per web query:
      - GET /system/health          (get_api_v1_system_health)          web useQuery(getExtendedHealth)
      - GET /dev-tools/runtime-info (get_api_v1_dev_tools_runtime_info)  web useConnectionPool
      - GET /system/version         (get_api_v1_system_version)          web useQuery(getVersionInfo)
    All three generated operation ids verified present in Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs. No HTTP in the view.
  * BackendStatusSection.Model.cs — null-tolerant JSON adapters; BackendHealthSnapshot (components map +
    embedded system block), ConnectionPoolSnapshot (max_open/open/in_use/idle/wait_count, exact Go wire
    field names verified in internal/api/devtools/handler.go), VersionSnapshot; the getStatusIcon /
    statusTextClass status→StatusKind+glyph mapping; the formatUptime port; the okCount badge variant; three
    result mappers; registration (id=backend-status-section, slug=BackendStatusSection); PII-safe diagnostics.
  * BackendStatusSection.ViewModel.cs — INotifyPropertyChanged state holder; folds the three streams into one
    section state (loading/loaded/empty/error/stale/offline). The combined skeleton mirrors the web
    isLoading = extLoading || poolLoading via sticky per-query "resolved" flags (TanStack isLoading semantics:
    true only until first settle, never on refetch). Snapshot retention avoids content flicker on refresh.
  * BackendStatusSection.cs — TsAccordion (Expander, defaultOpen) header = backend glyph + title + description
    + "{ok}/{total} healthy" TsBadge + TsDataFreshness; body switches on state: loading skeleton (live region),
    TsQueryError + retry, TsEmptyState, or the three sub-sections — Component Health (TsDataTable-style grid:
    status glyph+tone / component / latency / failures coloured red when >0 / last-check), Database Connection
    Pool (five TsStatCards), System Runtime (TsKVList). Each sub-section renders its own friendly empty surface
    (never hidden). Every string via ILocalizer; AutomationProperties.SetName on every data row, the badge and
    interactive elements; decorative icons set to AccessibilityView.Raw.
  * All UI-free logic (parse / projection / state machine / i18n keys / diagnostics) is unit-tested headlessly;
    the WinUI view is exercised by the app build (step [1]).

